{
 "$comment": "The Universal Wallet's declarations (lib/wallet.js). A wallet DEFINITION is a versioned blueprint in a namespace: its names (any language, any aliases), the value classes it may hold (Value's classes — lib/seed/value.json), the operations it allows (the operations below, plus hold), and its policy. A wallet INSTANCE belongs to an owner, holds one unit of value and binds one definition version; an owner may hold any number of wallets, named as they like. Money moves only as balanced, immutable ledger journals; a wallet's balance is a projection of its postings. Nothing here names a business: a definition is data, added in the console or the seed. Policy: overdraft (how far below zero available may go), max_balance (0: none), max_wallets_per_owner (0: any number), hold_minutes (how long a hold keeps value when its caller names no expiry).",
